Create and manage user-local strap sessions.

Usage:
  strap session new "repo analysis"
  strap session copy "alternate direction"
  strap session copy "alternate direction" --at bm_abc
  strap session resolve "repo analysis"
  strap session ask "Analyze this repo"
  strap session show
  strap session save < state.json
  strap session list
  strap session path
  strap session state
  strap session trace

Each session has its own overlay under `overlay/` and its own jj history. Session mutations create jj commits automatically. Session-aware commands require `STRAP_SESSION`; if it is absent, they fail.

In Nushell, `strap session select <session>` sets `$env.STRAP_SESSION`; without an argument it opens `sk` to choose a session interactively.
